ensure_none(df, amount < 0)   # 1 row: -5
ensure_all(df, amount >= 0)   # 2 rows: -5 and NA
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

Use \code{ensure_all()} when a value has to be present \emph{and} right, and
\code{ensure_none()} when a missing value is acceptable or is a separate rule
with its own message.

Several conditions must all hold, so a row is a violation when any of
them is \code{FALSE} or \code{NA}.
}
